## Recovered local application

- Requires Node.js 22 or newer. Run `npm ci` to install the locked dependencies for PDF generation and deployment. The local server itself uses Node built-ins; PDF creation uses pdf-lib and fontkit, bundled locally with esbuild.
- Run `npm start` from this repository, then open http://127.0.0.1:8787. Use `PORT=8788 npm start` if the default port is occupied.
- Run `npm test` for inventory/API tests and `npm run check` for JavaScript syntax checks.
- The [HTML interface](./html/index.html) lists all 210 drawers as large touch-friendly results with number, position, title and description. Search also covers tags and remarks. Selecting a result previews its source photo on the right. Select exactly one drawer and click **Edit** to edit title, description, tags and remark without losing the photo preview.
- Search also accepts a complete numeric range such as `90-96`, showing drawers **090 through 096 inclusive**. Leading zeros and spaces around the hyphen are accepted (`090 - 096`). Equal endpoints select one drawer; reversed ranges show no results. Other queries retain the existing case-insensitive, all-words text search. Select visible drawers can select the filtered range for PDF export; existing hidden selections are retained and counted.
- The accidental-editing PIN/session lock has been removed. **Edit** is available only when exactly one drawer is selected and the backend permits writes. Cloudflare Access and server-side validation are unchanged; a genuinely read-only backend still disables editing and saving. No browser session storage is required.
- Photos are visually transcribed from the supplied images, not sent to an external OCR service. Full-resolution originals remain in [photos](./photos); optimized display copies are in [html/images](./html/images). JSON `photo` paths are relative to the HTML directory. `sourceLabel` retains the initial reading and is not changed when editing inventory fields.
- Edits save after ten seconds without typing anywhere in the editor, including search. Typing in another drawer or searching postpones all pending autosaves. Save now bypasses the delay. Failed saves require Save now to retry. Spaces and newlines are stored exactly; tags are comma-separated and spaces in each tag are preserved.
- Full screen shows request progress, synchronizes the button after successful entry/exit, and reports stalled requests after five seconds. F11 is the browser-level fallback; it is separate from the page Fullscreen API.
- The photo preview is shown only for exactly one selected drawer. With zero or multiple selections it is empty, without a message, and photo upload is disabled. A single selected drawer without a photo shows `dummy.jpg`.
- The server writes [drawers.json](./drawers.json) atomically. Ordinary text patches change only the four editable fields; the dedicated image-upload endpoint can also change one drawer's photo path. Concurrent changes to the same field are rejected with an explicit conflict, not silently overwritten. Edits remain in the browser on failure; use Save now to retry network failures. On a conflict, export your draft, reload, and reconcile the changed fields.
- Export JSON downloads the current inventory including unsaved edits. Reload asks before discarding drafts. Leaving the page with unsaved edits triggers the browser's warning; drafts are not automatically recovered after closing the browser.
- Stop the server before externally replacing or regenerating the JSON. Multiple browser tabs are supported through field-level conflict checks, but independent processes directly writing the file do not share the server's write queue.
- The server binds only to 127.0.0.1 and rejects foreign hosts/origins. It is not a public production backend.
- Multipage label PDF downloads are available; print them at Actual size (100%), not Fit to page.

## Touchscreen layout, selection and label draft

- The UI uses real HTML controls and CSS grids, not an SVG overlay. It fits the available browser viewport at 100% zoom: the permanently visible keyboard occupies the bottom **30%**; the upper **70%** uses **65% width** for search/actions/results/editing and **35%** for the photo, with margins. There is no visible page title or whole-page scrolling. Results and editing fields scroll independently; the photo remains visible while selecting and editing.
- In normal view, the viewport excludes browser controls and the Windows taskbar, regardless of taskbar position. **Full screen** uses the browser Fullscreen API and switches to **Exit full screen**; Escape restores the normal view and button label. If unavailable or denied, an explicit message suggests F11. No fixed 1920 x 1080 CSS size or manual zooming is required.
- Large results show number, position, title and wrapped description. Photo display preserves the complete image and its aspect ratio (portrait images remain portrait). The photo remains available even if its drawer is filtered out. Touching it asks **New Image of THIS drawer only?**; Cancel changes nothing, OK opens the PNG/JPG file picker. **New image of this drawer** offers the same action, including when no photo is available.
- Checkboxes toggle individual drawers. Tapping the result selects just that drawer; Ctrl/Cmd-click toggles it, Shift-click selects a range, and Ctrl/Cmd+Shift adds a range. Shift ranges contain only the current search results. Physical keyboard Space toggles a focused result button; Enter selects it.
- **All visible** selects/deselects visible results; hidden selections remain selected and counted explicitly. **Clear** clears all checked drawers. **Edit** requires exactly one selection, including hidden selections, and shows all four editable fields in the upper-left panel. **Done** returns to results without discarding drafts or cancelling autosave. Autosave waits for ten seconds without typing, including search; **Save now** saves immediately.
- The permanent three-row Belgian AZERTY touch keyboard works with Search and the focused edit field. It has 20 grid tracks per row, including wider function keys and a spacer before the four-column numpad: `- 7 8 9` / `. 4 5 6` / `0 1 2 3`. The dedicated hyphen allows range searches without switching to symbols. At approximately 24 x 12 cm fullscreen, letter/number keys are about 1 cm with 2 mm gaps. They scale with the actual viewport; OS scaling affects physical size.
- **Shift** affects the next letter/symbol and resets; keypad digits and punctuation do not consume Shift. **Caps Lock** stays active and is red only when on. **#+=** toggles accented letters and symbols, including a hyphen for range searches and apostrophes; **ABC** returns to letters. Backspace deletes a selection or one Unicode grapheme; Space and textarea Enter preserve exact text. Search Enter and **SEARCH** return to results and focus search. Touch keys preserve input focus and caret; `inputmode="none"` requests suppression of the native touch keyboard without disabling physical typing.
- **More** retains PDF download, JSON export, Reload, Save now, optional USB connect/disconnect and print guidance without crowding the main buttons.
- **Download labels.pdf** creates one PDF page per selected drawer in inventory order, including selections hidden by filtering. It snapshots current values, including unsaved edits, without saving inventory. Every download requests the filename `labels.pdf`; the browser decides whether to replace an existing file or add a suffix.
- Labels are exactly **50 mm wide x 30 mm high**, with a white background and **1.5 mm inset print area**. The approved layout has a **46 x 9 mm** title box at (2, 2), centred bold title lines at y=6/10, uppercase description lines at (2, 16/19), a bold drawer number at (2, 28), and right-aligned position at (48, 27). Coordinates are millimetres measured from the top-left. Title wraps to 18 characters per line and description to 27, both limited to two lines with `...` for overflow. Tags and remarks are not printed; stored drawer text is untouched.
- All PDF text uses embedded **Noto Sans Mono Regular/Bold** (original font sizes retained), supplied locally under the SIL Open Font License in [html/fonts/LICENSE](./html/fonts/LICENSE). No external font service or PDF service is used. Missing fonts, download failures and unsupported characters produce an explicit error instead of a broken download.
- [html/label.js](./html/label.js) shares wrapping and content validation between editable SVG generation and the PDF renderer in [html/label-pdf.js](./html/label-pdf.js). `npm run build:labels` builds the ignored browser bundle; start, tests and Cloudflare build/deploy commands build it automatically.
- PDF regression tests cover exact page dimensions, embedded fonts, wrapping/truncation, invalid records, unsupported glyphs and font-fetch errors. Prior browser checks covered hidden selections, draft export, repeat downloads, single-page output, empty selection and font-error retry. A three-page generated PDF was rendered and checked against the approved layout; all 210 records exported successfully at that point.
- [label-template.svg](./label-template.svg) is the initial drawer-101 example to adapt in Vectorcraft and return as the next template.
- Keyboard tests cover the approved grid/numpad arrangement, Shift/Caps behavior, cursor insertion and replacement, Unicode Backspace, whitespace/newlines and field-length errors. Inventory/API tests retain conflict detection, exact text preservation and localhost restrictions. Browser editing checks use an isolated mock inventory rather than writing to the real drawer data.

